      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "WE WALK BY FAITH (9) was far from disgraced when he came from the back row for fourth to topliner Minstrel last time. Draws out so may need some luck but had won three of his previous four outings here, two of them from big handicaps. He is talented enough to overcome the barrier. CYCLONE JORDY NZ (8) has been mixing his form and was a touch disappointing last week but was terrific from the outside barrier when fourth in the Golden Nugget three back. His A-game would take him close. ULTIMATE MIKI (5) won from a wider barrier here three back and has been solid since so deserves respect. FABULOUS DREAM NZ (2) came from wider for a second-up win last week, taking her strike rate at this circuit and distance to 50 per cent. Harder here but she is aided by a low draw.",
